hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8416","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “The banner of the treacherous person will be raised for him on the Day of Resurrection, when people gather from the ancients and the last, and it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so, the son of \"So-and-so\""
"8417","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: An-Nadr bin Shumail told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I heard Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Every treacherous person will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so.”"
"8418","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Rifa’ah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Amr Ibn Al-Hamq Al-Khuza’i said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever believes in a man for his blood, and then kills him, is carrying a banner of treachery.” on the Day of Resurrection\""
"8419","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Umayrah told us, on the authority of Rifa’ah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Hamq, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever believes a man against himself, then... He killed him, and he will be given a banner of treachery on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"8420","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Qurrah, he said: Abdul-Malik told us, and Ya’qub told us Ibn Ibrahim, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Qurrah bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik Bin Umair, he said: Aamir Bin told me Shaddad, he said: Amr bin Al-Hamq told us, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “If a man is at ease with another man, then He killed him, and a banner of treachery will be raised against him on the Day of Resurrection.” And the wording is for Jacob."
"8421","Abdul Rahman bin Ibrahim Duhaim informed us, he said: Marwan informed us, he said: Al-Hasan, who is Ibn Amr, told us, Al-Hasan told us on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Junada bin Abi Umayyah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever kills a person from the people of the Dhimmah, He did not smell the fragrance of Paradise, and indeed its fragrance is felt from a distance of forty years.”"
"8422","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: Ismail informed us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Al-Araj, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath bin Thurmalah, on the authority of Abu Bakra He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever kills a person who has made a covenant without fulfilling it, God will forbid him from Paradise from even smelling its fragrance.”"
"8423","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Al-Hajjaj told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever kills a soul by making a treaty without its right, will not smell the scent of Paradise, and its scent is found from A journey of five hundred years.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is an error, but the correct thing is the hadith of Ali bin Ulayya, and Ibn Ulayya is more steadfast than Hammad bin Salamah, by God. I know, and Hammad bin Zaid is more steadfast than Hammad bin Salamah."
"8424","Mujahid bin Musa reported, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Samurah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “O Abd al-Rahman bin Samurah, do not ask for leadership, for if you give it to her for a request and are entrusted to her, even if You gave it to her without asking, you helped her.”"
"8425","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: Two men from the Ash’arites came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they began to offer work, so the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Indeed, the most trustworthy of you in my eyes is the one who sought him out, but he did not seek their help for anything.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8426","Muhammad ibn Adam informed us, on the authority of Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “You will strive for leadership, but it will be a matter of regret and regret on the Day of Resurrection. What a good breastfeeding woman, and how miserable she is.” \"Al-Fatima\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8427","Humayd bin Masada informed us, on the authority of Bishr, on the authority of Ibn Awn, on the authority of Umair bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent him as a messenger, and when he returned, he said: “How did you find yourself?” He said: I did not stop until I thought that he had been given permission to me, and bye. God, I cannot do anything on two legs as long as I live. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is Umair bin Ishaq. We do not know that anyone narrated from him, other than Ibn Aoun and Nabih al-Anizi. We do not know that No one narrated on his authority, other than Al-Aswad bin Qays."
"8428","Abdullah bin Abdul-Samad told me, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdul-Wahid, on the authority of Al-Mu’affa bin Imran, on the authority of Abdul-Hamid bin Jafar, He said: Sa`id al-Maqbari told me, on the authority of Ata’, the servant of Abu Ahmad. He said: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He greeted a group of people, called them, and began to say to the man: “What do you have of the Qur’an, O so-and-so?” He said: Such-and-such, so he recited it to them, until He passed by a man with them who was one of the youngest in age, and he said: “What do you have with you, so-and-so?” He said: Such-and-such, and Surat Al-Baqarah, so he said to him The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Do you have Surah Al-Baqarah?” He said: Yes. He said: “Go, for you are their prince.” A man from their nobles said: Oh Messenger of God, by God, nothing prevented me from learning the Qur’an, except for the fear that I would fall asleep and not get up with it. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “ Learn the Qur’an, so recite it and sleep, for the likeness of the Qur’an to one who learns it, reads it, and performs with it is like a sock stuffed with musk, which smells Its scent comes from every place, and it is like one who smells it, and it lies in his stomach like a sock, like a musk.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ishaq ibn Abd al-Wahid: I do not know him, and Abdullah ibn Abd al-Samad told us, on the authority of al-Mu’affa ibn Imran Without a hadith, we only took it out to include it between him and Maafia, and it was narrated by someone other than Abd al-Hamid bin Ja`far, so he sent it and the famous Sent (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8429","Muhammad bin Khalid told us, he said: Bishr bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mut’im was It is narrated that Muawiyah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “This matter is among the Quraysh. No one will be hostile to them except that God will suppress him.” His face is as long as they establish the religion.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8430","Imran bin Bakkar al-Homsi told us, he said: Ali bin Ayyash told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Abu al-Zinad told me, from what Abd told him. The Most Gracious Al-Araj, from what was reported, is that he heard Abu Hurairah speaking, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: And he said: “The imam is only a shield. He fights behind it, and fears it. If he commands to fear God and be just, he will have a reward for that, but if he commands something else, then it is upon him.”"
"8431","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed told me, he said: Baqiya told us, he said: Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hussein, on the authority of Al-Qasim Ibn Muhammad, he said: I heard my aunt Aisha saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever among you is assigned a job and God intends good for it, He appointed for him a good minister. If he forgets, he reminds him, and if he remembers, he helps him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8432","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: I asked Suhail bin Abi Salih, I said: Hadith Amr told us, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’, About your father? He said: I heard it from the one who was told by my father. A man from the Levant, called Ata’ bin Yazid Al-Laythi, told me on the authority of Tamim Al-Dari. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The religion is advice, the religion is advice.” They said: To whom, O Messenger of God? He said: “To God, to His Book, to His Prophet, to the Imams of the Muslims, and to their common people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8433","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Shuaib bin Al-Layth narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “The religion is sincere advice. Advice, religion is advice. They said: To whom, O Messenger of God? He said: “To God, to His Book, to His Messenger, to the Imams of the Muslims, and to their common people.”"
"8434","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Ibn Wahb reported, saying: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul-Rahman, On the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “God has not sent a prophet, nor appointed a caliph, except that it was He has two entourage: an entourage that commands him to do good and urges him to do it, and an entourage that commands him to do evil and urges him to do it, so the infallible is the one who is infallible. \"God\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8435","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told me, he said: Muammar bin Yamar told us, he said: Muawiyah told me, meaning Ibn Salam, he said: he told me Al-Zuhri said: Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no guardian but his Two friends: a friend who commands him to do good and forbids him from evil, and a friend who does not deceive him, so whoever is protected from its evil is protected. He is one of those who prevail over him from both of them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8436","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, on the authority of Shuaib bin Al-Layth, on the authority of Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Jafar He said: Safwan told me, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, he said: I heard the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God has not sent A prophet, and there was no caliph after him, except that he had two companions: an companion who commanded him to do good and forbid evil, and a companion who did not deceive him with deception. “Whoever is protected from the lining of evil has been protected.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8437","Amr bin Ali reported, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Asim Al-Adawi, on the authority of Ka’b Ibn Ujrah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There will be princes, so whoever believes their lies and helps them to Their injustice is not from me, and I am not from it, and it does not come to my coffin, and whoever does not believe them in their lies, and does not help them in their injustice, is from me. And I am from him, and he comes to my basin.”"
"8438","Muhammad bin Al-Ala told me, he said: Abu Khalid, who is Sulayman bin Hayyan, told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’a’, he said: I said to Abdullah bin Omar: We will go to our princes, so I will say: a word, and when we leave from them, we will say something different. He said: “ We considered this to be hypocrisy during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8439","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Waki` reported, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Fudayl bin Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Nayyar, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “We do not seek help from a polytheist.”"
"8440","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Fudayl bin Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Nayyar On the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will not seek help from a polytheist.”"
"8441","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Hushaym told us, saying: Mansour reported, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that a woman from among the Muslims She was captured by the enemy, and before that they had attacked a camel belonging to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she saw that some of the people were unaware, so she mounted. The camel of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she made a vow over it. God saved her from slaughtering it, so she came to Medina and wanted to To slaughter the camel of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but she was prevented from doing so, so that was mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “ “Evil is your reward.” Then he said: “The son of Adam does not make a vow regarding what he does not possess, nor regarding disobedience to God Almighty.”"
"8442","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik told me, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Abu al-Ghaith, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Khaybar, and Muhammad said: The year of Khaybar, and we did not take any spoils except wealth. And the goods and clothes. A man from Banu Ad-Dhubayb, called Rifa’ah bin Zayd, presented a gift to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a black boy. It is said to him: a supporter. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, headed to Wadi Al-Qura, until they were in Wadi Al-Qura while a supporter was landing. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when an arrow came to him and struck him, killing him. Then the people said: Congratulations to him in Paradise, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “No, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the spear that he took from the spoils of Khaybar on the Day of Khaybar was not struck by the cuts, so that it would catch fire.” Fire upon him.\" When the people heard that, a man brought one or two traps to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He, peace and blessings be upon him: “One or two traps of fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8443","Amr bin Ali and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ reported, saying: Yazid told us, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ma’dan bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Thawban, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “Whoever’s soul separates from the body and is innocent of three things will enter Paradise: treasure, and in the hadith of Muhammad: arrogance, deceit, and debt.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8444","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam reported, saying: Ishaq Abu al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Suleiman bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded a commander in charge of a company or an army, he would advise him only for himself. With fear of God and with the believers and Muslims, and he said: “Fight in the name of God, and in the path of God. Fight and do not exceed, do not mutilate, and do not betray And do not kill a newborn. If you meet an enemy from among the polytheists, call them to three, and whichever of them they respond to you, accept. From them, and desist from them: Invite them to Islam, and if they answer you, then accept from them, and desist from them, then invite them until they convert. From their home to the home of the emigrants, and tell them that if they do that, they will have what the emigrants owe, and they will have what the emigrants owe, even if They refused to move to the home of the immigrants, so tell them that they will be like the Arabs of the Muslims, and God’s judgment will apply to them as they It applies to the believers, and they do not have anything in the spoils or in the spoils, except that they wage Jihad with the Muslims, for if they refuse, So ask them to pay the tribute, and if they do, then accept from them and desist from them. If they refuse, then seek help from God and fight them. You besieged the people of Hisn, and they asked you to grant them the protection of God and the protection of your Prophet, but do not grant them the protection of God or the protection of your Prophet. But assign to them your obligation, the obligation of your father, and the obligation of your companions, for if you betray your obligation and the obligation of your fathers, it will be easier for you. If you have violated the protection of God and the protection of the Messenger of God, then if you besiege the people of a fortress and they ask you to submit them to the judgment of God, then do not You put them down to the rule of God, but put them down to your rule, for you do not know whether you will follow God’s rule in them or not.” Alqamah said: I narrated this hadith to Muqatil bin Hayyan, and he said: Muslim bin Haysam Al-Abdi narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Muqrin, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, likewise (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8445","Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala reported, saying: Ibn Wahb reported, saying: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, that Al-Maswar ibn Makhramah told him that Amr ibn Awf, an ally of Banu Ammar ibn Luayy, had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah to Bahrain to bring its tribute, and the Prophet had prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He reconciled with the people of Bahrain, and appointed Al-Ala’ bin Al-Hadrami over them, so Abu Ubaid came forward with his money from Bahrain. The Ansar heard of the arrival of Abu Ubaidah, so they performed the dawn prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed He left, and they confronted him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, smiled when he saw them and said: “I think you have heard that Abu Ubaidah Did he come with anything from Bahrain? They said: Yes. He said: Give good news and hope for what pleases you. By God, there is no poverty for you. I fear for you. I fear for you that the world will be extended to you, as it was extended to those before you, so you will compete in it as they competed, and it will destroy you. just as You destroyed them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8446","Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: He told me. Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah told him that Amr ibn Awf had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He informed him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah to Bahrain to bring its tribute. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made peace with the people of Bahrain, and appointed Al-Ala’ bin Al-Hadrami over them. Abu Ubaidah came with money from Bahrain, so the Ansar heard of his arrival, so she performed the dawn prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed The Fajr prayer, upon him be peace and blessings, left, and they confronted him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, smiled when he saw them and said: “I think you have Did you hear that Abu Ubaidah came, and he brought something? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “So give good news, and hope for what pleases you. By God, it is not poverty that I fear for you, but I fear for you that the world will be extended to you, as it was extended to those before you. So compete with her as they competed with her, and she will distract you as she distracted them.”"
"8447","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim reported, saying: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Amr, who heard about his bravery, “Umar did not take tribute from the Magians, until he witnessed Abdul Rahman bin Awf, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it from the Magians of Hajar.”"
"8448","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Abdul Rahman told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: Abu Talib fell ill, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to visit him. There was a man sitting at his head, so Abu stood up. Out of ignorance, he sat in it, so they complained to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Abu Talib, and they said: This applies to our gods, so he said: O son of my brother, what do you want? To this? He said: “Uncle, I only want them to accept a word that the Arabs will owe them, and then the non-Arabs will pay the tribute to them.” So he said: What is it? He said: “There is no god but God.” So they said: Make the gods one god. This is a strange thing. And the crowd of them departed. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8449","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Abdullah bin Omar al-Qurashi told us, he said: Saeed told me Ibn Amr Ibn Saeed, that he heard his father claiming, that he heard his father on the Day of Marj, saying: I heard Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, saying: Had I not I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God will prevent this religion from the Christians of Rabi’ah on the shore of the Euphrates. I have not left an Arab except I kill him or he surrenders.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Abdullah bin Omar Al-Qurashi: This I do not know. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8450","Suleiman bin Dawud reported, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa bin al-Zubayr, that Hisham bin Hakim bin Hazzam found a man while he was in Homs sunbathing with Nabatean people while they were paying tribute, and he said: What is this? I am the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “Indeed, God punishes those who torture people in this world.”"
"8451","Amr bin Mansour reported, saying: Al-Hakam bin Nafi’ told us, saying: Shuaib reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, saying: Sinan bin Abi Sinan Al-Du’ali told me, And Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, that Jabir bin Abdullah told them that he had launched a campaign with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Before Najd, when the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered, he entered with him, and the one who said, one day, meaning in a valley full of biters, overtook them, so the Prophet descended. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the people dispersed among the trees, seeking shade from the trees. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, descended under the shade of a tree and clung to it. His sword. Jabir said: So we slept, then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called us. We answered him, then a Bedouin was sitting with him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This man pierced my sword while I was sleeping, so I woke up with a prayer in his hand, so he said: Who will prevent you? From me? I said: God. He said: Who will prevent you from me? I said: God. He said: Who will prevent you from me? I said: God. He drew the sword and sat down, and did not The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, will punish him, and he has done that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8452","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported, reading from him, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik told me, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned from a campaign, or Hajj, or Umrah, he would say “Allahu Akbar” three times on every corner of the earth. Then he says: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner, to Him belongs dominion, and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. “Prostrate, thankful to our Lord. God has fulfilled His promise, supported His servant, and defeated the parties alone.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8453","On the authority of Mahmoud bin Ghaylan, on the authority of Abu Dawud, and Yahya bin Adam, both on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Subaie’i, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned from a journey, he would say: “You will repent.”"
"8454","Yazid bin Muhammad bin Abd al-Samad al-Dimashqi told me, he said: Abu Mushar told us, he said: Yahya bin Hamza told me, he said: he told me Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, said: Abd al-Rahman bin Ka’b bin Malik told me, he said: I asked the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And his companions: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray the morning rosary? They did not confirm anything about that, except that they mentioned that it was: “When he came from a journey, the Ma`ras would come down until he entered the forenoon, and begin In the mosque, he kneels in it two rak'ahs, then sits until the Muslims around him come to him and greet him, then he rises to \"His wives\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8455","Anba Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Asim told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Ibn Shihab told us, that Abd al-Rahman bin Abd Allah bin Ka'b bin Malik told him, on the authority of his father Abdullah bin Ka'b, and on the authority of his uncle Ubaid Allah bin Ka'b, on the authority of Ka'b bin Malik, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “would not set out from a journey except during the day and at noon, so when he came, he would start with the mosque and pray two rak’ahs therein.” Then he sat in it.”"
"8456","Suleiman bin Dawud informed me, he said: Ibn Wahb informed me, he said: Yunus informed me, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me, and Abd al-Rahman bin informed me. Ka'b bin Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ka'b, said: I heard Ka'b bin Malik, narrating his hadith when he fell behind. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose in the morning.” May God bless him and grant him peace. Whenever he came from a journey, he would come to the mosque and pray two rak’ahs there, then he would sit in front of the people."
"8457","Yusuf bin Saeed told me, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: Laith told us, he said: Aqeel told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abdul told me Al-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Ka’b, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik, said: I heard Ka’b bin Malik narrating his speech when he fell behind. On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: When he came to Medina, “the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque and prayed,” brief, On the authority of Amr ibn Yazid, on the authority of Bahz ibn Asad, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar al-Sadusi, on the authority of Jabir (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8458","Muhammad bin Maadan bin Issa bin Maadan told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Ayan told us, he said: Maqil told us, and he is Ibn Ubaid Allah, On the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik told me, on the authority of his uncle Ubayd Allah bin Ka’b, he said: I heard my father Ka'b narrates, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rarely wanted a face unless he saw another face, until the Battle of Tabuk took place, so he rose The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made his matter clear to the people there, and he wanted the people to be prepared for their attack.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8459","Muhammad ibn Jablah and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Harrani told me, saying: Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Ayan told us, he said: My father told us, On the authority of Ishaq bin Rashid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Abu Ka’b ibn Malik saying: He was one of the three upon whom he repented. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rarely He would launch a campaign unless he knew about it, and Muhammad said: Other than that, until the Battle of Tabuk took place, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up. So he made his matter clear to the people there, and he wanted the people to be prepared for their invasion.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8460","Bishr bin Hilal Al-Basri reported, he said: Ja’far, meaning Ibn Sulaiman, told us, he said: Harb bin Shaddad told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, launched the Battle of Tabuk, he left Ali in Medina. They said about him: He bored him and hated his company. So Ali followed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, until he caught up with him on the road, and he said: O Messenger of God, you succeeded me. In Medina with the children and women, until they said: He bored him and hated his company, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “O Ali, I only left you in charge of My family, are you not satisfied to be to me what Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8461","Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kufi reported, saying: Abu Usama reported, on the authority of Burayd, who is Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of his father, he said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came from Hunayn, he sent Abu Amir with an army to Awtas, where he met Ibn al-Sammah and was killed, and God defeated him. His companions, Abu Musa said: Abu Amir was shot in the knee, and a man from Banu Jashm shot him with an arrow, which pinned him to his knee. So I came to him and said: Uncle, who shot you? Abu Amer pointed to Abu Musa and said: That is my killer. You see, he is the one who shot at me. Abu Musa said: So I went to him and supported him. So I followed him, and when he saw me, he turned away from me, so I followed him and started saying to him: Aren’t you ashamed? Aren't you an Arab? Don't you stand firm? ! He thought, so he and I met, and we struck each other, so I struck him with the sword and killed him, then I returned to Abu Amer, and I said: I have God killed your friend. He said: Take this arrow. So I took it out, and water gushed out of it. He said: O son of my brother, go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, so extend my greetings to him, and tell him: lest he say to you: Ask forgiveness for me. He said: Abu Amer appointed me as his successor over the people, so he stayed For a little while, then he died, and when I returned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, I entered upon him, and he was in a house on a made-up bed, with a mattress on him. The sand from the bed affected the back of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his sides, so I told him our news, and he told Abu Amir, so I said: He said to me: Tell him: Ask forgiveness for me. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for water for me, so he performed ablution, then raised his hands and said: “O God, forgive.” To Ubaid Abi Amer, “until I saw the whites of his armpits,” then he said: “O God, make him superior to many of Your creation or people on the Day of Resurrection.” So I said: By me, O Messenger of God, so ask forgiveness. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, forgive Abdullah bin Qays his sin, and let him enter.” On the Day of Resurrection, an honorable entrance.” Abu Burdah said: One of them is by Abu Amer, and the other is by Abu Musa. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8462","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told me, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Shu’bah bin Al-Hajjaj, On the authority of Alqamah ibn Marthad al-Hadrami, on the authority of Suleiman ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that when He sent an emir to command a company or an army, and he gave special instructions to himself to fear God, and to be good to those who were with him among the Muslims. Then he said: “Invade in the name of God.” God, and in the cause of God, fight whoever disbelieves in God. Fight, and do not betray, and do not exceed, and do not mutilate, and do not kill a child, for if you You meet your enemy among the polytheists, so invite them to one of three times. Whichever of them they have not responded to you, accept from them, and desist from them: Invite them to convert to Islam. If they do, accept from them and desist from them. Then invite them to convert from one house to another. The immigrants, and if they do so, tell them that they will have the same rights as the immigrants, and they will have the same duties as the immigrants, if they convert to Islam. And they chose their home, so tell them that they will be like the Bedouins of the Muslims, and the same ruling that applies to believers will apply to them, and it will not be They have nothing in the spoils and spoils, except that they wage jihad with the Muslims. If they refuse, then invite them to pay the tribute. If they do, So accept from them and desist from them, and if they refuse, seek God’s help against them, then fight them, and if you besiege the people of a fortress, So they wanted that you should make them follow the rule of God, so do not make them follow the rule of God, but make them follow your rule, for you do not know whether you will be correct. What is God’s ruling on them? And if you besiege the people of a fortress and they want you to assign to them the protection of God and the protection of His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. So do not assign to them the protection of God and the protection of His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, but assign to them your protection, the protection of your father and the protection of your companions. If you conceal your debts, the debts of your fathers, and the debts of your companions, it is easier for you than to conceal the obligation of God and the obligation of His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"8463","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “Travelling is a piece of torment. It deprives one of you of his sleep, food, and drink. So when one of you fulfills his voracious appetite, his face is Let him hasten to his family.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8464","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Malik told us, and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Malik, he said: Sumayy told me, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Travelling is a piece of torment. “One of you abstains from his appetite, his food, and his drink.” Ibn al-Muthanna said: “And his drink. If one of you has fulfilled his hunger, let him return to his family.” Ibn Al-Muthanna said: Let him hasten to his family. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8465","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, Ibn Jurayj said: Muammar told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Ka’b, on the authority of his grandfather, said that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “went out in the Battle of Tabuk on Thursday, and he loved to go out in \"on Thursday\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8466","Muhammad bin Maadan bin Issa told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Ayan told us, he said: Maqil told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abdul told me Al-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik, on the authority of his uncle Ubaid Allah bin Ka’b, who said: I heard Abu Ka’b bin Malik say: The Messenger of God God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “Rarely does he want one face without seeing another face, until the Battle of Tabuk took place, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rose So he made his matter clear to the people, and he wanted the people to be prepared for their attack, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became an invader on the day of “Thursday,” abbreviated (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8467","Suleiman bin Dawud told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Ka’b told me, On the authority of his father, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rarely went out on a journey, for jihad or otherwise, except on Thursdays.”"
"8468","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: Aws bin Abdullah bin Buraidah told me, he said: Al-Hussein bin Waqid told me, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, bless my nation in their firstborns.”"
"8469","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “was forbidden to He travels with the Qur’an to the enemy’s land, fearing that the enemy will attack him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8470","Saeed bin Abdul Rahman reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: And provide for food, for the best food supply is piety. He said: “There were people who performed Hajj without food.” So it was revealed: And food food, for the best food food is piety."
"8471","Muhammad bin Adam told me, he said: Abdah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Wahb bin Kaysan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, He said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent us as a group of three hundred carrying our provisions on our necks. Then our supply increased, until a man had all of us.” A day of dates, so we came to the sea, and behold, there was a whale that had been thrown up by the sea, so we ate from it for eighteen days.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8472","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik told us, on the authority of Wahb bin Kaysan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a delegation before the coast, and Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah commanded over them, and they were three hundred, and I Among them, we went out until we were on some road, and the supplies ran out, so Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah ordered the supplies for that army, and all of them were gathered. So he was my provider of dates, and we used to feed them little by little every day, until it was no longer available, and only one date after another was enough for us. So I said: What is the benefit of one date? He said: We found it lost when it was exhausted, then we went to the sea, and behold a whale like a swarm, and that army ate eight of it. For ten nights, then Abu Ubaidah ordered that two of its sides be erected, and they were erected. Then he ordered a mount, and it departed, then it passed under them, and it did not \"You hit them\""
"8473","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told me, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Al-Muttalib bin Hantab Al-Makhzoumi told me, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Amra al-Ansari told me, he said: My father told us, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a battle. So the people were struck by starvation, so the people asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, permission to slaughter some of their backs, and he said: God will inform us of it, so when Omar bin Al-Khattab saw that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was about to give them permission to slaughter some of their backs. He said: O Messenger God, how will we be when we meet the people tomorrow, hungry men? But if you decide, O Messenger of God, to invite the people with the remains of their blood, So you collect them, then pray for blessing in them, for God will inform us of your supplication, or He said: He will bless us in your supplication, so the Messenger of God called God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with the remains of their provisions, so he made the people come, meaning a large portion of food, and on top of that, the highest of He brought a saa' of dates, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered them. Then he got up and supplicated for what God wished for him to supplicate, then he called the army. With their containers, and he ordered them to dig, and there was not a container left in the army that they did not fill, and another like it remained, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed. peace be upon him until his molars became visible, and he said: “I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that I am the Messenger of God. No servant who believes in them will meet God.” Unless the Fire will be hidden from him on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"8474","Abu Bakr bin Abi al-Nadr al-Baghdadi told us, he said: Abu al-Nadr Hashim bin al-Qasim told us, he said: Ubayd Allah al-Ashja’i told us. On the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted on his way. He said: The people ran out of supplies. He said: So they were about to slaughter some of their camels. Omar said: O Messenger of God, if you gathered what Some of the people's provisions remained, so I prayed to God to save them, and he did so. Then he brought Dhu Al-Birr with his wheat, and Dhu Al-Tamar with his dates. He said: And Mujahid said: And the ones with the nuclei have their nuclei. He said: So I said: What did they do with the nuclei? ! He said: They sucked it and drank water over it. He said: So he prayed over it until the people filled their jugs, and then he said: “I bear witness that it is not There is no god but God, and I am the Messenger of God. No servant will meet God with them without doubting them except that he will enter Paradise. Musa bin Abdul Rahman told us, He said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Malik, who is Ibn Mughal, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Abu Salih, who said: “While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he greeted him on his way, when the people ran out of supplies.” He mentioned the hadith as mursal."
"8475","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Musab bin Abdullah told us, he said: Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Suhail, On the authority of Suleiman Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “came out on a campaign that he fought, and he was wounded.” His companions were hungry and their supplies were exhausted, so they came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complaining to him about what had befallen them. They asked him for permission to sacrifice some of their camels, so he gave them permission, so they went out, and they passed by Omar bin Al-Khattab, and he said: Where did you come from? So they told him that they had asked permission from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to slaughter some of their camels. He said: So he gave you permission. They said: Yes. He said: So I ask you, and I swear to you, not to return with me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so they returned with him. So Omar went to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, do you permit them to sacrifice their camels? What should they ride? God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “So what do you do, I do not have what to give them? He said: “Rather, O Messenger of God, you order someone who has some extra food to come to you, and you collect it for something, and you pray for it, and then you divide it up.” He did so among them, so he called them by virtue of their provisions. Some of them brought a little or a lot, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed him for something. Then he called for what God wished for him to call for, then he divided it among them, and not one of the people remained but he filled what he had of a container, and some left over. Then he said: “I bear witness that there is no god but God alone, with no partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God who brought it on the Day of Resurrection.” Without doubt, admit him to Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8476","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Qatada bin Al-Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: We went out With the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a Umrah or a campaign. We camped at a certain place, and a man from among the people came and said: O Messenger of God, if We slaughtered some of our backs, and the polytheists saw our good condition, so he said: “Whatever you want.” Then Omar came and said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Gather. Give them more, so pray to God. The people brought their supplies of flour, dates, and barley. He prayed for them and said: “I am in charge of your supplies.” So they came. With it, they endured as long as God wished, and there was much bounty among them. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am the servant of God, and I am the Messenger of God.” By God, whoever brings it will not be blocked from Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8477","Musa bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, he said: Burayd bin Abdullah bin Abi Burdah told me, on the authority of his grandfather, my father. Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the Ash’arites become widows during the battle, the food for their families becomes scarce.” In the city, they collected what they had in one garment, then they divided it among them in one vessel equally, so they are of me, and I am of them.”"
"8478","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ali Ibn Rabi’ah, he said: I witnessed Ali coming with an animal. To ride her, and when he put his foot in the stirrup, he said: In the name of God. When he sat on her back, he said: Praise be to God, then he said: Glory be to God. He who has subjected this to us, and we would not have said it, and indeed, to our Lord we will return. Then he said: Praise be to God three times, and God is great three times. My Lord, I have wronged myself, so forgive me, for no one forgives sins except You. And he said again: Glory be to You, I have wronged myself, so forgive me. No one forgives sins except you. Then he laughed. I said: At what did you laugh, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing as I did, then he laughed. I said: At what did you laugh, O Messenger of God? He said: “Indeed, your Lord admires His servant when he says: Forgive me my sins. He knows that no one forgives sins except Him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8479","Muhammad ibn Qudamah reported, saying: Jarir told me, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ali ibn Rabi’ah al-Asadi, he said: I saw Ali coming With an animal, and when he put his foot in the stirrup, he said: In the name of God. When he sat on it, he said: Praise be to God who has subjected this to us and we were not to Him. And indeed to our Lord we will return. Then he said “Allahu Akbar” three times, and thanked God three times, then he said: “There is no god but You. Glory be to You. Indeed, I have wronged myself.” So forgive me my sins, for no one forgives sins except you. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said one day like what I said, then He laughed, so I said: Why did you laugh, O Messenger of God? He said: “Our Lord marvels at His servant’s saying: Glory be to You. Indeed, I have wronged myself, so forgive my sins. Indeed, no one forgives sins except You. He said:” My servant knows that he has a Lord who forgives sins.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8480","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi reported, on the authority of Hammad, who said: Asim told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sargis, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was When he travels, he greets him and says: “O God, you are the companion on the journey, and the successor to the family. O God, accompany us on our travel, and succeed us in our family. O God, I seek refuge in You from the hardships of travel, the gloom of a turning point, from the turmoil after despair, the supplication of the oppressed, and the bad outlook in life. \"family and money\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8481","Muhammad bin Umar bin Ali bin Muqaddam reported, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Bishr al-Khathami, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, travelled, he would ride his mount. He said, with his finger, and extended He raised his finger and said: “O God, you are the companion on the journey, and the successor to the family. O God, increase the land for us, and make the journey easy for us. Oh God, I seek refuge in You from the hardships of travel and the depression of a turning point.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8482","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, on the authority of Mu`tamir, on the authority of his father, that a man narrated to him, on the authority of Abu al-Sawwar, who narrated to him, on the authority of Jundub ibn Abdullah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he “sent a group, so he sent Abu Ubaidah over them, and when he set out, But he cried in his youth to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he sent a man in his place, called: Abdullah bin Jahsh, and he wrote a letter, And he commanded him to turn his face away, and he commanded him not to read the letter until he reaches such-and-such, and do not force any of your companions to Walking with you. When he read the letter, he recovered, then said: “In listening and obedience to God and His Messenger,” so he told them the news and read to them the letter. Two men returned, and the rest of them went on, and they found Ibn al-Hadrami and killed him. They did not know whether that day was Rajab or Jumada, so he said The polytheists to the Muslims: You did such-and-such and such-and-such in the sacred month, so they came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him the hadith. Then God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: They ask you about the sacred month, to His saying: And sedition is greater than murder and polytheism. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8483","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, and another mentioned, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah On the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a detachment while I was among them. He said: If you meet so-and-so And so-and-so, they burned them with fire. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, bade farewell to us, he said: “I commanded you to burn them with fire, and it is not He must be punished with the punishment of God, so if you meet them, kill them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8484","Amr ibn Uthman told me, on the authority of Al-Walid, on the authority of Hanzala ibn Abi Sufyan, that he heard Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad say: I was with Ibn Umar. When a man came to him to bid him farewell, Ibn Umar said to him: Wait, I bid you farewell, just as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to bid farewell to us: “I bid farewell to God. Your religion, your trustworthiness, and the end of your work.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8485","Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Muhammad informed us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Khuthaym, he said: Hanzalah told us, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah bin Omar, he said: Whenever my father saw a man who was about to travel, he would say: Bring him near so I may bid you farewell, just as the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, used to bid us farewell. Then he would say: “Entrust to God your religion, your trust, and the end of your work.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8486","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zur, on the authority of Ibn Masoud said: On the day of Badr, there were three of them riding a camel, and the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Ali bin Abi Talib, and Abu Lubabah, and when he was at his back, they would say: Ride until we walk. Then he would say: “You are not stronger than me, and I am not without reward.” \"from both of you\""
"8487","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, that a man from the Ansar He told him that he was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on some of his travels, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a messenger: “No.” “They leave a string necklace on the camel’s neck, unless it is cut.” Malik said: “I see that from the eye.”"
"8488","Abu Al-Ash'ath reported, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Sa'id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “He ordered the bells to be rung.”"
"8489","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8490","Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Maan told us, he said: Malik told us, and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us the recitation of it and the pronunciation for it. On the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Abu al-Jarrah, the client of Umm Habibah, on the authority of Umm Habibah, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The caravan in which there is a bell is not accompanied by angels.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8491","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Al-Alaa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “The bell is one of the psalms of Satan.”"
"8492","Wahb bin Bayan told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, that Ibn Shihab told him, on the authority of Salem Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Safinah, the slave of Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Do not accompany angels. A package containing a bell.”"
"8493","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir reported, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “When you travel for the sake of fertility, give the camels their share of the land, and when you travel for the year, then travel quickly for them, and when “When you set out at night, avoid the road, for it is a haven for vermin at night.”"
"8494","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: While the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace, regarding some of his Companions, when a man among them cursed his camel, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who is cursing his camel?” The man: It is me, O Messenger of God. He said: “Then delay it on our behalf, for it is obligatory.”"
"8495","Muhammad bin Muammar Basri told us, saying: Abd al-Malik bin al-Sabbah told us, on the authority of Imran, who is Ibn Hudayr Basri, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Abi Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that a woman was riding a camel, and she became fed up, so she cursed her, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Throw away her belongings, for she is cursed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8496","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Zakaria informed us, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Jabir, that he was walking with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was upon him and greeted a camel, but it became tired and wanted to let it go. He said: “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, overtook me, so he called for it and struck it. He said So he walked a walk like no other. He said: Will you sell it to me for an uqiyah? And the uqiyah is forty dirhams. He said: I said: No. He said: Will you sell it to me? With an uqiyah, and I excluded his lambs for my family. When we reached the level, I brought him the camel, and he gave me its price. Then I came back, and he sent for me and said: “You see? I did not cover you to take your camel? “Take your camels and your dirhams, and they are yours.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8497","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Raqqashi told us, he said: Rafi’ bin Salamah bin Ziyad told me, he said: told me Abdullah bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Ja’il Al-Ashja’i, said: I fought with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in some of his campaigns, and I was on A mare of mine was lean and weak. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, caught up with me and said: “Go, owner of the horse.” I said: O Messenger of God, it is lean. She was weak, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, picked up a whisk that he had with him and hit her with it, and said: “O God, bless him with it.” He said: I saw that I could not control her head in front of people. He said: I sold her belly for twelve thousand. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8498","Ahmad bin Saeed told us, he said: Ishaq told us, meaning Ibn Mansour, he said: Zuhair told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abdullah Al-Awdi, On the authority of Wabara Abu Karz al-Harithi, on the authority of Rabi’ ibn Ziyad, he said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was walking, he saw a boy from A young man of Quraysh was walking away from the road, and he said: “Isn’t he so-and-so?” They said: Yes, he said: “Call him.” They said: They called him, and he said: “Why did you step out of the road?” He said: I hate dust. He said: “Do not turn away from it, for by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, it is an offspring of Paradise.” Abu Dawud reported. He said: He told us. Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ayan, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Dawud bin Abdullah Al-Awdi told us, that Wabra Abu Karaz told him, He heard Rabia bin Ziyad say: “While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was walking, he passed by a boy from Quraysh,” and something similar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8499","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Waki` told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: There was panic in Medina, So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, borrowed a horse of Abu Talha’s, called Mandub, and he rode it. He returned and said: “We did not see any terror. And if We find it to be a sea.”"
"8500","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Muadh bin Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father He was one of the emigrants, and he said: “The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not fly away from anything, but when he was asked about the man’s name, he would Good, the good news was seen on his face, and if it was bad, that was seen in him, and if he was asked about the name of the land, it was good, it was seen. The good news is on his face, and even if he is bad, that is seen in him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8501","Abdah bin Abdullah reported, on the authority of Suwayd, who is Ibn Amr Al-Kalbi, on the authority of Zuhair, who is Ibn Muawiyah, who said: Asim Al-Ahwal told us, Trustworthy and trustworthy, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: Abu Musa told me, saying: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, so he treated the people On a valley, so they shouted “Allahu Akbar” (God is great), there is no god but God, and Asim raised his voice, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Oh! O people, be careful with yourselves. Indeed, the one whom you call upon is not deaf. Indeed, he hears and is near. He is with you. He repeated it three times. Abu said. Musa: Then he heard me say while I was behind him: There is no power nor strength except in Allah. So he said: “O Abdullah bin Qais, shall I not direct you to a word from among the treasures?” Paradise? I said: Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. He said: There is no power nor strength except in God. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8502","Amr bin Ali and Bishr bin Hilal told us, and the wording is his. They said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abu Musa. Al-Ash'ari said: The people gathered around an obstacle or a bend, and whenever a man ascended it, he called at the top of his voice: There is no god but God, and God Greater, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You will not call a deaf person or an absent person.” Then he said: “O Abu Musa, shall I not guide you to treasures?” Paradise? “I said: Yes. He said: “You say: There is no power nor strength except in God.”"
"8503","Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Sadran Al-Basri reported, on the authority of Khalid bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Jabir said: “When we were with The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was on a journey, so we ascended and said “Allahu Akbar,” and when we descended we said “Allahu Akbar.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8504","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Naysaburi, known as al-Farra, informed us, he said: Ayoub ibn Sulayman told us, he said: Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Abu Suhail bin Malik, on the authority of his father, that he used to listen to the reading of Omar bin Al-Khattab, while he was leading the people in the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him from the house of Abu Jahm, and Ka’b al-Ahbar said: By the one who parted the sea for Moses, because Suhayb told me that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When he saw a village he wanted to enter, he said: “O God, Lord of the seven heavens and what they overshadow, and Lord of the seven earths and what We have diminished, by the Lord of the devils and what they have led astray, by the Lord of the winds and what they have caused. Indeed, we ask you for the good of this town and the good of its people, and we seek refuge in protect you from the evil of it, the evil of its people, and the evil of what is in it.” Ka’b swore by the one who divided the sea to Moses, for these were the supplications of David when he saw the enemy. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8505","Amr bin Sawad bin Al-Aswad bin Amr reported, saying: Ibn Wahb reported, saying: Hafs bin Maysarah informed me, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Marwan, on the authority of his father, that Ka’b narrated to him, that Suhayb, the companion of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, narrated to him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, narrated to him that He, peace and blessings be upon him, never saw a village he wanted to enter except that he said when he saw it: “O God, Lord of the seven heavens, and what they cast over, and Lord of the seven earths, and what We have diminished, by the Lord of the devils, and they have not led us astray, by the Lord of the winds, and we have not abandoned. Indeed, we ask you for the good of this town and the good of its people. We seek refuge in You from its evil, the evil of its people, and the evil of what is in it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8506","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala reported on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: He also told me, meaning Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that when the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was on a journey, he would say: “The one who hears praises God and his good affliction.” upon us, our Lord, our Companion, and bestow blessings upon us. We seek refuge with God from the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8507","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was the best of people. The most generous of people, and the bravest of people, he said: The people of Medina were terrified one night when they heard a voice, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, met them riding a horse. Abu Talha was naked, and he was girding his sword, so he said: “You were not heeded, you were not heeded.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I found it at sea.” Meaning: the horse (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8508","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Baja bin Badr al-Juhani, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The best thing that people have ever lived for is a man holding the reins of his horse in the path of God. Whenever he hears a sound or panic, he flies on Aboard his horse, he sought death and killing in his place, or as a man in one of these branches, or in the depths of a valley of these. valleys as a spoil for him. He establishes prayer, pays zakat, and worships God, until certainty comes to him. He is not among people but in the best.”"
"8509","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abdul-Malik bin Nawfal bin Musahiq told us, He said: I heard Ibn Issam Al-Muzani, on the authority of his father, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a convoy, he said: “If you see mosque, or you hear a muezzin, so do not kill anyone.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8510","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, and another mentioned, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah, On the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a troop, and I am among them. He said: “If you meet so-and-so And so-and-so, burn them with fire.” Then when the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, bade farewell to us, he said: “Indeed, I commanded that you burn them with fire, and it should not be To be punished with the punishment of God, so when you meet them, kill them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8511","Amr bin Ali reported, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ya’la bin Ata’, on the authority of Amara bin Hadid, on the authority of Sakhr Al-Ghamidi, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Oh God, bless my nation with its firstborn.” And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He sent a company, sent them out early in the day."
"8512","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, and I hear, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Omar bin Malik told me, and another before him mentioned, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ja`far, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Salman al-Aghar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered a secret group to go out They said: O Messenger of God, shall we go out tonight, or shall we stay until morning? He said: “Do you not like, meaning, to spend the night among the sheep of Paradise?” And the sheep: the garden."
"8513","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik told me, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Salih Al-Samman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Were it not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would love not to fall behind.” About a group that goes out for the sake of God, but I cannot find anything to compel them to do, and they do not find anything to support them with, and it is difficult for them to remain behind. After me, I wished to fight in the cause of God and be killed, then come back to life and be killed, then come back to life and be killed, then come back to life and be killed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8514","Abdah bin Abdullah narrated, saying: Zayd bin Hubab narrated, saying: Muhammad bin Salih narrated to us, saying: Husayn bin Abdul Rahman narrated to me, He said: I and Hafs bin Ubaid Allah bin Anas entered upon Anas bin Malik while he was standing praying, so he stood for a long time, then sat down, so I said: O father, do you not know this? He said: Who is this? So I attributed it to him, and he cried until he gasped, then said: I heard a hadith from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and if I had narrated it one day in the past, I would have narrated it. Today: We, together with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, invaded Tabuk, so he sent Khalid ibn al-Walid with forty riders to Ibn Dumat al-Jandal. So he said: “If you are able to take him, then take him, and do not kill him, but if you are not able to take him, then kill him.” So they came to his palace, and he said His family: He had not been out for two months before today, and we found him shooting game, but we were unable to take him, so we killed him, so they came With an armor that had brocade on it, he went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions marveled at it. He said: “Do you marvel at the Are these the handkerchiefs of Saad bin Muadh softer than those in Paradise? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8515","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Abu Usama told us, he said: Abu Ruq Atiya bin Al-Harith Al-Hamdhani told us, he said: Abu Al-Gharif told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Assal, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent us in a expedition, and he said: “Proceed in the name of God in For the sake of God, you fight the enemy of God, and do not commit excesses, and do not commit treachery, and do not mutilate, and do not kill a newborn.”"
"8516","Saeed bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Nawfal bin Musahaq, on the authority of Ibn Issam, on the authority of his father, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent an army or a troop, he would say to them: “If you see a mosque, or hear a muezzin, do not “You kill someone.” So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent us a detachment and ordered us to do so. We went out walking in the land of Tihama, and we overtook a man. He was driving lizards, so We offered him Islam and said: Are you a Muslim? He said: What is Islam? So we told him, and if he did not know it, he said: If I do not do it, what will you do? We said: We will kill you. He said: Are you waiting for me until I catch up with the oppressors? We said: Yes, and we are overtaking you. So he went out and came to a woman who was wearing her howdah and said: Surrender Hubaysh before the end of livelihood. Aslam ten times, and eight times, and seven times, then he said: Do you remember when I looked at you and found you wearing jewelry, or I met you? In the gorges, was it not true that a lover who took the trouble of bringing in secrets and documents should die? Is it not my fault? I said, “When we were brought together together, I will be rewarded with a connection before One of the servants greeted Ethibi cordially before the hearts grew cold and the prince moved away from the departed beloved. Then he came to us and said: What is your business? So we presented him. So we beheaded him, and the other woman descended on him from her howdah and felt compassion for him until she died. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8517","'Imran ibn Bakkar ibn Rashid informed me, saying: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, saying: Shu'ayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: 'Amr ibn Abi Sufyan ibn Usayd ibn Jariyah al-Thaqafi — who was one of the companions of Abu Hurayrah — informed me that Abu Hurayrah said:\n\n\"The Prophet ﷺ sent a detachment of ten men as a scouting party, appointing over them 'Asim ibn Thabit al-Ansari, the grandfather of 'Asim ibn 'Umar ibn al-Khattab. They set out until they were at al-Hudah, which is between 'Usfan and Makkah. They were mentioned to a tribe of Hudhayl called Banu Lihyan. About a hundred archers hastened toward them. They tracked their tracks until they found their food — dates they had provisioned from Madinah. They followed their tracks. When 'Asim and his companions saw them, they took refuge in a rocky elevation, and the people surrounded them. They said to them: 'Come down and give us your hands, and you shall have our covenant and pledge that none of you will be killed.' 'Asim ibn Thabit, the commander of the detachment, said: 'As for me, by Allah, I shall not today place myself under the protection of a disbeliever. O Allah, inform Your Prophet ﷺ about us.' They shot them with arrows and killed 'Asim along with seven others. Then three men came down under the covenant and pledge, among them Khubayb al-Ansari, ibn Dathinah, and another man. When they had them in their power, they loosed the bowstrings and bound them. The third man said: 'This is the first betrayal. By Allah, I shall not accompany you.' They dragged him and tried to compel him, but he refused to accompany them, so they killed him.\n\nThey set out with Khubayb and ibn Dathinah until they sold them in Makkah after the Battle of Badr. Khubayb was purchased by the Banu al-Harith ibn 'Amir ibn Nawfal ibn 'Abd Manaf. Khubayb was the one who had killed al-Harith ibn 'Amir on the day of Badr. Khubayb remained with them as a captive. 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas informed me that the daughter of al-Harith told them that when they had gathered, he (Khubayb) asked her for a razor to shave with, and she lent it to him. She said: 'A young son of mine crawled, while I was unaware, until he reached him.' She said: 'I found him upon his thigh, with the razor in his hand. I became alarmed with an alarm that Khubayb recognized in my face. He said: \"Do you fear that I would kill him? I would never do that.\" She said: 'By Allah, I have never seen a captive better than Khubayb. I found him one day eating from a cluster of grapes in his hand, while he was bound in iron, and there was no fruit in Makkah.' She used to say: 'It is indeed a provision from Allah that He has provided to Khubayb.'\n\nWhen they went out from the Sacred Precinct to kill him in the non-sacred territory, Khubayb said to them: 'Allow me to perform two rak'ahs of prayer.' They left him, and he performed two rak'ahs. Then he said: 'Were it not that you would think I am afraid, I would have added more. O Allah, count them all.' He then recited:\n\nI care not, when I am killed as a Muslim,\nOn which side my fall shall be for Allah.\nAnd that is in the essence of Allah, and if He wills,\nHe may bless the limbs of a dismembered body.\n\nThen Abu Sirwa'ah 'Uqbah ibn al-Harith arose and killed him. Khubayb was the one who established the practice of the two rak'ahs for every Muslim killed in a state of patience. Allah, the Almighty, the Majestic, answered the supplication of 'Asim ibn Thabit on the day he was killed. The Prophet ﷺ informed his companions of their news on the day they were killed.\n\nSome men from the disbelievers of Quraysh were sent to 'Asim when they were told he had been killed, to bring back something of him by which he could be recognized, for he had killed one of their leaders on the day of Badr. Allah sent upon 'Asim a cloud-like cover of hornets, which protected him from their messenger, so they were unable to cut any piece of his flesh.\""
"8518","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya Al-Qattan told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, and Marwan ibn Al-Hakam, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out some time ago. Al-Hudaybiyyah with some ten hundred of his companions, until they were in Dhul-Hulayfah. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, imitated the sacrificial animal, and felt, He entered into ihram for the Umrah, and sent his servants from Khuza’ah to tell him about the Quraysh. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked until he was At Ghadir al-Ishtāt, near Usfan, Utbah al-Khuza’i came to him and said: I have left Ka’b ibn Luayy, and Aamir ibn Luayy have gathered for you. The Abyssinians, and they gathered a group of people against you, and they were fighting you and repelled you from the House. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Admonish me. Do you think I will turn? To the descendants of those who helped them, they will be their share. If they betray, they will be treacherous. They will remain dead, and if they will survive, they will be a neck that has been severed. By God, or do you think that I should lead the House, and whoever turns us away from it, we will fight him.” Abu Bakr said: God and His Messenger know best, O Prophet of God. We came to perform Umrah, and we did not come to fight anyone, but whoever came between us and the House, we will fight him. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “So go away.” So, brief (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8519","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria reported, saying: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, and Sufyan bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, On the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who brings us the news of the people?” Al-Zubayr said: I do, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “For every prophet there is a disciple, and my disciple is Al-Zubair.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8520","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Ibn Wahb reported, saying: Sa`id bin Abdul-Rahman told me, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the Day of the Trench: “Who is the man who brings us news? Banu Qurayza? Al-Zubair said: I do, so he went on his horse and brought their news, then he said the second time, so Al-Zubair said: I did, then he went. Third, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is Al-Zubair.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8521","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, saying: Suleiman bin Harb told us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, He said: Wahb bin Kaysan said: I bear witness that I heard Jabir bin Abdullah say: When the situation became severe on the day of Banu Qurayza, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Who will bring us their news?” No one went, so Al-Zubayr went and brought their news. Then the matter became more severe, so the Prophet said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Who will bring us their news?” No one went, so Al-Zubayr went. Then the matter became more severe, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: “Who will bring us their news?” No one went, so Al-Zubayr went and brought their news, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: “Indeed, every prophet has a disciple, and Al-Zubayr is a disciple.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8522","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Ja`far bin Aoun told us, saying: Abu Umays reported, on the authority of Iyas bin Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, on the authority of his father, saying: A group of polytheists came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was camping. When he tasted it, he slipped away, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ali is the man, kill him.” Then the people rushed to him and said: “My father was in a hurry to outrun the horse, so he overtook them and caught him by the muzzle of his camel. So he killed him, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, plundered him."
"8523","Abu Dawud narrated, he said: Ya’qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd informed me. Allah ibn Utbah said that Abdullah ibn Abbas informed him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to Caesar inviting him to Islam. He sent his letter with Dihya al-Kalbi, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to deliver it to the chief of Busra, so that he could deliver it to the governor of Busra. Caesar, so the Azim of Busra gave him to Caesar, and when Caesar was revealed by God to the soldiers of Persia, he walked from Homs to Ilia in thanks for what God made him successful. When Caesar brought the letter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said when he read it: Seek, is there anyone here among his people? To ask him about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace?, brief."
"8524","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of the letter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. To Khosrau, Ibn Shihab said: Ubayd Allah told me that Abdullah bin Abbas told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace “He sent his letter to Khosrau, and ordered him to deliver it to the Grandmaster of Bahrain, so the Grandmaster of Bahrain delivered it to Khosrau,” he said. When Khosrau read it, he tore it up.”"
"8525","Yusuf bin Hammad told us, he said: Abdul Ala told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “ Before his death, he wrote to Chosroes, to Caesar, to the Negus, and to every tyrant, calling them to God Almighty, not the Negus who prayed. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"8526","Humayd ibn Masada narrated on the authority of Bishr, who is Ibn al-Mufaddal, who said: Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God wanted God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, asked him to write a letter to the Romans, and they said: “They do not read a letter unless it is sealed.” So he took a silver seal. It is as if I were looking at the whiteness of it in his hand, and engraved on it: Muhammad is the Messenger of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8527","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The rider is a devil, and the two riders are two devils, and the three are riders.”"
"8528","Al-Mughirah bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Muhammad bin Rabi’ah told us, he said: Omar bin Muhammad Al-Amri told us, he said: On the authority of his father, On the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If people knew what is in a loneliness, a rider would never travel at night.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8529","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, and I hear, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of his father, that he heard his grandfather Abdullah bin Omar He narrates, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “If people knew about loneliness, I would not know if a rider traveled alone at night.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8530","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Suleiman told us, he said: Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sinan bin Abi Sinan al-Du’ali, that Jabir bin Abdullah al-Ansari told him that he had launched a raid with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, before Najd. Then one day the woman who said it met them in a valley full of brooks, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended, and the people dispersed in the brook, seeking shade. By trees, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended under a tree and stuck his sword to it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man He said to him: “This man pierced my sword while I was sleeping, and I woke up with a prayer in his hand.” So he said to me: Who will protect you from me? So I said: “God,” and he said to me: Who will prevent you from me? So I said: “By God,” and he drew the sword and sat down, and behold, he was sitting. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not punish him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8531","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar reported on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Jami’ bin Shaddad, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman Ibn Alqama, Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is in my book, and the correct thing is: Abdul Rahman bin Abi Alqama, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Masoud said: We arrived with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the time of Hudaybiyyah, and they mentioned that they descended trampling through the land, meaning By being trampled on by sand. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who will eat us?” Bilal said: It is me, O Messenger of God. He said: “Then you sleep?” So they slept until the sun rose, then some people woke up among them so-and-so and so-and-so, and among them was Omar. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, woke up and said: “Do as “You used to do it.” So we did. He said: “So do it for someone who fell asleep or forgot.” He said: The camel of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lost weight. So I looked for her, and I found that her rope was attached to a tree, so I brought her, and we rode, and when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended The revelation was upon him, and this became difficult for him, and we knew that about him, so he moved aside, withdrawing behind us, and began to cover his head, and it became difficult for him, until We knew that it had been revealed to him, so he came to us, so he informed us that it had been revealed to him. Indeed, We have opened for you a clear opening. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8532","Suwayd bin Nasr reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Al-Masudi, on the authority of Jami’ bin Shaddad, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Alqamah, he said: He said: Abdullah: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned at the time of Hudaybiyyah, he said: “Who is guarding us tonight?” Abdullah said: So I said: I, he said. “You are sleeping,” and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who is guarding us tonight?” He said: So I said: I am. He said: “You are sleeping,” then he said. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Who is guarding us tonight?” He said: And the people remained silent, so I said: I am. He said: “Then you?” He said: So I guarded them until, at dawn, they overtook me, as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. So I slept and did not wake up except for the sea. The sun is on our shoulders, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up and did as he used to do, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If God had willed That you do not sleep on it, you did not sleep on it, but God wanted it to be a Sunnah for those after you, for those who slept or forgot.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8533","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Yahya, he said: My father told me, that Abu Sa`id al-Khudri He told him that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in Al-Hudaybiyyah, he said: “Do not light a fire at night.” So when he was after that, he said: “ “Incite and create, for no people after you will realize your allowance or your supply.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8534","Amr bin Uthman told me, on the authority of Al-Walid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Ala bin Zubr, that he heard from Abu Ubayd Allah Muslim bin Mishkam, He says: Abu Tha’labah Al-Khushani told us, he said: Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, camped at a place, he would camp, and they would separate from him in the forests. And the valleys, so he stood among them and said: “Your dispersal among the paths and valleys is only from Satan.” So when they descended after that They joined one another, to the point that you say: If you had spread a covering over them, you would have covered them, or something like that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8535","Ali bin Al-Hussein told us, he said: Umayyah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, was digging the trench with us, and the dirt was on his stomach, and he was saying: “O God, had it not been for you, we would not have been guided, nor would we have given charity, nor had we prayed.” So send down a peace upon us. Indeed, the evil ones have transgressed against us when they wanted our father’s religion.”"
"8536","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Mu’tamar told us, he said: I heard Awf, he said: I heard Maimun speaking, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered us to dig the trench, he showed us a stone in it that the pickaxe cannot take, so we complained about that. To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, threw off his garment, took the pick, and said: “In the name of “God,” so he struck a blow, breaking a third of the rock. He said: “God is the Greatest. I have been given the keys to the Levant, and by God, I can see its red palaces now from This is my place,” he said: Then he struck another, and said: “In the name of God,” and broke another third, and said: “God is great, I have been given the keys of Persia. By God, I can see the White Palace of Medina now.” Then he struck a third time and said: “In the name of God.” He cut the stone and said: “God is great.” I have been given the keys of Yemen, and by God, I can see the door of Sana’a.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8537","Amr bin Ali and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported on the authority of Khalid, who said: Humaid told us on the authority of Anas, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out in A cold morning, while the Muhajireen and the Ansar, meaning they were digging the trench, said: “O God, the best is the best of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar.” And the emigrants answered him: We are the ones who pledged allegiance to Muhammad for jihad as long as we remain alive.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8538","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Zuhri told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Ibn Al-Munkadir told us, and I heard it and memorized it, He said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mourned on the Day of the Trench, so Al-Zubayr mourned, then they mourned. So Al-Zubayr delegated, then he delegated them, then Al-Zubair delegated, and said: “Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is Al-Zubair.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8539","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Muhallab bin Abi Safra, he said: A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke to me. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the night of the ditch: “I do not see people except “May you spend the night tonight, for your slogan is: ‘They will not be helped.’” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8540","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Ibn Wahb informed me, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told me, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Iyas bin Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, on the authority of his father, said: “We were with Abu Bakr on the night of our house at Hawazin. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us over us.” And peace be upon him, and our motto was: “Death, death.”"
"8541","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Alaa bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: I memorized it from Amr, he said: I heard Jabir, he said: We were With the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a battle, then a man from the immigrants kicked a man from the Ansar, and the Ansari said: Oh, the Ansar, and he said Al-Muhajiri: Oh the Muhajireen, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard about that, and he said: “What is the matter with the claim of pre-Islamic times?” They said: O Messenger of God. A man from among the immigrants stabbed a man from the Ansar. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave her, for she is stinking.” So he heard about that. Abdullah bin Ubai, who was with them in the raid, said: Or have they done it? By God, if we return to Medina, they will expel the most powerful. The most humiliating of them, so Omar stood up and said: O Messenger of God, let me cut off the neck of this hypocrite. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No.” He speaks, strike the neck of this hypocrite.” He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “People do not speak, that Muhammad kills his companions.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8542","Ibrahim bin Muhammad al-Taymi, the judge who was in Basra, informed us. He said: Yahya bin Sa`id al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of al-Hasan, On the authority of Utai, on the authority of Ubayy, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever offers consolation with the condolences of pre-Islamic times, give him a reward from his father, and do not \"Be ye\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8543","Muhammad bin Hisham Al-Sadusi told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Al-Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Ubayy, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says: “If one of them cherishes the consolation of the pre-Islamic period, then treat him with his father’s sacrifice, and do not be embarrassed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8544","Hisham bin Ammar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Shuaib told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salam told me, that his brother Zaid bin Salam told him, On the authority of his grandfather, Abu Salam, that he told him, he said: Al-Harith Al-Ash’ari informed me, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever called According to a pre-Islamic claim, he is from the bottom of Hell. A man said: O Messenger of God, what if he fasts and prays? ! He said: “Yes, and if he fasts and prays, then call upon the call of God with which God has bestowed upon you: Muslims, believers, servants of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8545","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Jami’ bin Shaddad, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Abi Alqamah said: Abdullah said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned at the time of Hudaybiyyah, he said: “Who will guard us tonight?” He said: So I said: I am. He said: “You are sleeping.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who is guarding us tonight?” He said: And the people remained silent, so I said: I, he said: “So you are now,” he said: So I guarded them, until when the dawn broke, I realized what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, So I slept, and we only woke up with the heat of the sun on our shoulders. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up and did as he used to do. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up and did as he used to do. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “If God had willed that you should not sleep over it, you would not have slept over it, but He wanted it to be a Sunnah for those after you, for those who slept or \"forgot\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8546","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir bin Rabi’ah, that Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stayed up one night when he arrived at Medina and said: “I wish a righteous man from among my companions would guard me.” Tonight.” He said: We were amazed at that, as we heard the rattle of a weapon. He said: “Who is this?” He said: Saad bin Abi Waqqas. So he said to him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “What brings you?” Saad said: Fear fell within me for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I came. I guarded him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for him, then he fell asleep."
"8547","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Thawr bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Aidh, on the authority of Mujahid bin Rabah, On the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Shall I not inform you of a night better than the Night of Decree, a sentinel in a land of fear? Perhaps he will not return to his family.” Muhammad said: Whenever Yahya narrated it in public, he would not raise it, and if he narrated it in private Especially his elevation (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8548","Al-Harith bin Miskin reported a reading on his behalf, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Abd al-Rahman bin Shurayh narrated to me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Shumayr, on the authority of my father Ali Al-Janabi, on the authority of Abu Rayhana, said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a campaign, and I heard him say: “Fire has been forbidden.” For an eye that shed tears from the fear of God, the Fire was forbidden for an eye that stayed vigilant in the path of God.” And I forgot the third, and I heard after that, he said: “Forbidden.” “The Fire is upon an eye that has turned a blind eye to what God has forbidden.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8549","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Muhammad told us, he said: Abu Tawba told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salam told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Salam, that he heard Abu Salam, he said: Al-Saluli told me that Sahl ibn Al-Hanzaliyyah told him that they traveled with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day Hunayn, so they went at a leisurely pace, until it was the evening of prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a horseman came and said: O Messenger of God, I set out in front of you until I came to such-and-such mountain, and behold, I was at a barracks right next to them, next to them. Their livestock and their wives gathered together at Hunayn, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, smiled and said: “This will be the spoils of the Muslims tomorrow. God willing.” Then he said: “Who will guard us tonight?” Anas bin Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi said: “I am, O Messenger of God.” So he said: “Ride.” So he mounted his horse and came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Meet this people.” So that you may be at its highest level, and we will not be deceived by you tonight.” When morning came, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to his place of prayer, and he bowed down. Two rak'ahs, then he said: \"Have you made your knight feel good?\" A man said: O Messenger of God, we have not made him feel good. So he prayed, and the Messenger of God made While he was praying, God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, turned to the people, until when he had finished his prayer, he greeted him and said: “Rejoice, your knight has come.” So we started to look through the trees in the path, and behold, he came, until he stopped by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I have set off. Until I was at the top of this mountain where the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded me. When I woke up in the morning, I climbed both sides and looked, but I did not see anything. Uhud, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Did you come down tonight?” He said: No, except for a person praying or fulfilling a need. He said: “It has It was obligatory for you, so you do not have to do it after this.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8550","Ali bin Shuaib Al-Baghdadi reported, he said: Ma’n told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Saifi, the freedman of Ibn Aflah, on the authority of Ibn al-Sa’ib, the freedman of Hisham bin Zahra said that he entered Abu Sa`id al-Khudri’s house and said: I found him praying, so I sat waiting for him to finish his prayer. So I heard movement under his bed in his house, and I saw a snake, so I got up to kill it. Abu Saeed indicated to me: Sit down, so I sat down. When the people left, he pointed to a house in the house and said: Do you see this house? I said: Yes, and he said: There was a young man among us who had an engagement at a wedding, so we went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the ditch. That young man used to ask for permission in the middle of the day to see his family, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked permission one day, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: May God bless him and grant him peace: “Take your weapon, for I fear for you, Qurayza.” So the man took his weapon, then left, and he saw his wife. She was standing between the two doors, so he prepared a spear for her to stab her with, and jealousy struck him, so she said: Stop your spear until you can see what is in your house. So he went in and saw a snake folded on his bed. He stuck his spear into it and it was placed in it. Then he went out and set it up in the house. Then the serpent was struck by the tip of the spear, and the boy fell down dead. So it is not known which of the two died faster, the boy or the serpent? So we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we mentioned that to him, and we said: O Messenger of God, pray to God for us to revive him, and he said: Ask forgiveness for your friend.” Then he said: “Indeed, in Medina there are jinn who have converted to Islam, so whoever of them appears to you, pronounce him three times, and if he returns, kill him.” \"He is a devil.\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8551","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Al-Abbas Al-A’ma, on the authority of Abdul Allah bin Amr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, besieged the people of Taif, as if he had not gained anything from them, so he said: “We are standing still.” God willing. Then the Muslims said: Shall we go, but it did not open? ! He said: “Morning to fight.” They did so in the morning, and they were wounded. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “We are standing still.” It was as if they were They desired that, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed."
"8552","Ubaid Allah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Wahb bin Jarir, he said: My father told us, he said: I heard Harmala speaking, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Deaconess, he said: I entered upon Aisha, and she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “O God, whoever has appointed me in charge of the affairs of my nation, So be kind to them, so be kind to him.”"
"8553","Yahya bin Uthman told us, he said: Baqiya told us, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdul Allah ibn Umar said that he heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “Every shepherd is responsible for his flock. The Imam is a shepherd and responsible for his flock.” Brief (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8554","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Count “I have the one who speaks Islam.” So we said: Do you fear for us when we are between six hundred and seven hundred? ! Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You do not know, perhaps you will be tested.” So we were tested, to the point that one of us was made to pray only in secret."
"8555","Harun bin Musa Al-Farwi told us, he said: Muhammad bin Falih told me, on the authority of Musa, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Urwa told me, that Marwan Al-Miswar bin Makhramah told him that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him permission to free the Banu Hawazin, he said: I do not know who among you has given permission and who has not given permission. So return until your officials bring your matter to us.” So the people returned, and their officials spoke to them. So they returned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8556","Ubayd Allah bin Sa`id told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: Nafi` told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God bless him and grant him peace, “He visited him on the Day of Uhud, when he was fourteen years old, but it was not permissible for him to do so. He also visited him on the Day of the Trench, when he was five years old.” Ten, so he allowed him.”"
"8557","Ubaid Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of my father Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “One of the prophets attacked his companions, and he said: A man who built a house who did not He lives there, or he married a woman with whom he did not have intercourse, or he has a need to return, so he met the enemy when the sun was setting, and said: Oh God She is commanded, and I am commanded, so detain her for me until she judges between me and them. So God imprisoned her for him, so he opened for him, so they gathered The spoils, but the fire did not consume them. He said: And when they took a spoil, God would send fire upon it, and it would consume it. So their Prophet said to them: You have made a mistake, so let a man from every tribe come to me and pledge allegiance to me. So they came to him and pledged allegiance to him. The hand of two of them stuck to his hand, so he said: They said to them: Indeed, you have bound them, and they said: Yes, we bound an image of a cow's head made of gold, so they brought it, and they threw it to the spoils, so he sent The Fire was upon it, and it consumed it. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said at that: “Indeed, God fed us the spoils out of mercy with which He bestowed mercy upon us.” And He made it easy for us, when He knew of our weakness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8558","Muhammad bin Yahya Abu Ali reported, saying: Ali bin Al-Hakam Al-Marwazi told us, saying: Rafi’ bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hashraj bin Ziyad, on the authority of His grandmother, his father’s mother, said: I went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the battle of Khaybar, and I was the sixth of six women. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reached God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said that he had women with him, so he sent for us, so we came to him, and we saw anger on the face of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. So he said to us: “What brought you out, and by whose command did you come out?” We said: We went out, O Messenger of God, with you, handing arrows, watering the trees, and seeking treatment. The wounded, and we spin the hair, helping with it for the sake of God. He said: “Arise, and depart.” She said: When God conquered Khaybar for His Messenger, he contributed shares for us. Like men's arrows. He said: So I said to her: O grandmother, what did I do to you? She said: Dates (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8559","Muhammad bin Zanbour al-Makki reported, saying: Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Umm Atiyya, who said: “I marched with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went through seven battles. I followed them in their camps, prepared their food, and treated the wounded. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8560","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Bishr told us, he said: Khalid bin Dhakwan told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, she said: “We were fighting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, so we will give the people water, serve them, and return the wounded and the dead to Medina.”"
"8561","Bishr bin Hilal reported, saying: Ja`far bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to raid Umm Sulaim, and women from the Ansar with her, so they would give him water and treat the wounded.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8562","Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated, saying: Ahmad ibn Shabib narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Saeed bin Al-Musayyab and Abdul-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Ka’b told me that Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Indeed, God supports this religion with the immoral man.” Summary"
"8563","Imran bin Bakkar bin Rashid informed us, he said: Abu Al-Yaman told us, he said: Shuaib reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Saeed bin Al-Musayyab informed me, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God supports the religion of an immoral man.” Summary"
"8564","Muhammad bin Sahl bin Askar reported, saying: Abd al-Razzaq told us, saying: Rabah bin Zayd reported, on the authority of Muammar bin Rashid, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Anas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God supports this religion with people who have no morals.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8565","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Malik told us, he said: Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Nayyar, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out on a raid and invaded it, until such-and-such was the case, and a man from the polytheists followed him. It was severe, so they rejoiced over him. He said: O Messenger of God, I have come to be with you, and he was injured. He said: “We do not seek help from a polytheist.” He said that three times. Several times, he converted to Islam on the fourth day, and set off with him."
"8566","I am Al-Hussein bin Issa Al-Qumsi, he said: we are Affan bin Muslim, he said: we are Salam Abu Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: the Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He made women and perfumes beloved to me from this world, and he made the comfort of my eye in prayer.”"
"8567","Ali bin Muslim al-Tusi told us, he said: Sayyar told us, he said: Ja`far told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He made women and perfumes beloved to me, and he made prayer the comfort of my eye.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8568","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim, who is Ibn Tahman, told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: “There was nothing more beloved to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, than horses.”"
"8569","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of An-Nadr bin Anas, on the authority of Bashir bin Nahik, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever has two wives and prefers one of them over the other will come on the Day of Resurrection.” One of its parts is slanted.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8570","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Yazid told me, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told me, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Yazid, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to divide among his wives, and he would do justice, and then he would say: “Oh God This is my action regarding what I control, so do not blame me regarding what you possess, and I do not possess it.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Hammad ibn Zayd sent him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8571","'Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'd ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, saying: my paternal uncle narrated to us, saying: my father narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, who said: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed me that 'Aishah said:\n\n\"The wives of the Prophet ﷺ sent Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She sought permission to enter upon him while he was reclining with me in my outer garment. He gave her permission. She said: 'O Messenger of Allah, your wives have sent me to you, asking you for justice regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafah.' I remained silent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: 'O my daughter, do you not love what I love?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then love this one (i.e., 'Aishah).'\n\nFatimah stood up when she heard that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She returned to the wives of the Prophet ﷺ and informed them of what she had said and what he had said to her. They said to her: 'You have not availed us of anything. Go back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and say to him: Your wives implore you for justice regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafah.' Fatimah said: 'No, by Allah, I shall never speak to him about it again.'\n\n'Aishah said: The wives of the Prophet ﷺ then sent Zaynab bint Jahsh to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She was the one who used to rival me in status among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ. I had never seen any woman better in religion than Zaynab, more conscious of Allah, more truthful in speech, more dutiful to family ties, more generous in charity, and more humble of herself in the deeds by which she gave charity and drew near to Allah, the Almighty, the Majestic — except for a certain intensity of temper in her, from which she would quickly relent.\n\nShe sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with 'Aishah in her outer garment, in the same state in which Fatimah had entered. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her permission. She said: 'O Messenger of Allah, your wives have sent me to you, asking you for justice regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafah.' She attacked me at length, while I watched the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and watched his gaze, whether he would permit me to respond. Zaynab did not cease until I realized that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not dislike my defending myself. When she attacked me, I did not let her be until I had thoroughly responded. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'She is indeed the daughter of Abu Bakr.'\"\n\n'Imran ibn Bakkar al-Himsi informed us, saying: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, saying: Shu'ayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed me that 'Aishah said: And she mentioned something similar to it, saying: \"The wives of the Prophet ﷺ sent Zaynab. She sought permission and was given permission. She entered and said something similar to that.\" Ma'mar differed from them both, narrating it from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'Aishah."
"8572","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ al-Naysaburi, trustworthy and trustworthy, informed us, saying: Abdul Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha said: The wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered and sent Fatima to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said to her: Your wives, and he mentioned a word that means: They ask you for justice regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafa. She said: So she went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was With Aisha in her cloak, and she said to him: Your wives have sent me, and they are seeking from you justice for the daughter of Abu Quhafa. So the Prophet said to her, “Pray May God bless him and grant him peace: “Do you love me?” She said: Yes. He said: “Then love her.” She said: So I returned to them and told them what he had said to them. They said: You did not do anything, so go back to him. She said: By God, I will never go back to him about her. She was the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Indeed, they sent Zainab bint Jahsh. Aisha said: She was the one who was my equal among the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: Your wives sent me, and they are seeking justice for you regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafa. Then she came to me and insulted me, so I made I was watching the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and looking at his face. Would he give me permission to get rid of her? She said: She cursed me to the point that I thought he would not He hates me to get away from her, so I met her, and I did not have time to warm to her. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “She is the daughter of Abu Bakr,” Aisha said: “I have never seen a woman more charitable, more charitable, more connected to family ties, and more generous in everything for herself.” Through it he draws closer to God Almighty from Zainab, except for a severe Surah in which he was in, in which the calamity was about to come. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This Wrong, and the correct one before it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8573","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: We are Bishr, meaning Ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: We are Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The superiority of Aisha over women is like the superiority of porridge over other foods.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8574","Ali bin Khashram informed us, saying: I am Jesus, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The superiority of Aisha over women is like the superiority of porridge over all other foods.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8575","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, he said: We are Shadhaan, he said: We are Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Umm Salamah, do not trouble me about Aisha, for by God the revelation has not come to me in “The quilt of any woman from among you except her.”"
"8576","Muhammad ibn Adam told me, on the authority of Abdah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Awf ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Rumaitha, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the wives of the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He told her to speak to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that people were eager for gifts on the day of Aisha, and she would say to him: We love goodness as you love Aisha. So she spoke to him, but he did not answer her. When he went to her, she spoke to him also, but he did not answer her. They said: He did not respond. On you? She said: He did not answer me. They said: Do not leave him until he answers you, and you will see what he says. Then when he came to her the third time, she spoke to him, and he said: “Do not harm me in Aisha, for the revelation did not descend upon me while I was in the blanket of a woman among you, except in Aisha’s blanket.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8577","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdah bin Sulaiman, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ People were eager to give their gifts on the day of Aisha, seeking thereby to please the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: These two hadiths are authentic on the authority of Abdah."
"8578","Muhammad ibn Adam informed us, on the authority of Abda, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Salih ibn Rabi’ah ibn Hudayr, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was revealed to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I was with him, so I got up and closed the door between me and him. When he turned away from him, he said to me: “O Aisha, the Gabriel greets you with peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8579","Nuh bin Habib told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet prayed May God’s peace and blessings be upon him. He said to her: “Indeed, Gabriel recites his peace upon you.” I said: May God’s peace, mercy, and blessings be upon him. She sees what we do not see. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8580","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Al-Hakam bin Nafi’ told us, he said: Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah told me, that Aisha She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Aisha, this is Gabriel, and he is reciting peace upon you.” Likewise, he said Abu Abdul Rahman: This is correct, and the one before it was wrong, and on the authority of Ahmad bin Yahya bin Al-Wazir bin Suleiman, on the authority of Saeed bin Ufayr, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid bin Musafir, on the authority of al-Zuhri, with it"
